-- Heroic dungeon rows that do not exist: INSERT DUNGEON_HEROIC rows for 216 creatures that spawn in a 5-man heroic-capable instance (creature.spawnMask & 4)
-- and have a DUNGEON_NORMAL row but no DUNGEON_HEROIC row (non-combat triggers/stalkers/friendly NPCs and rows that would equal the fallback are left out).
-- Cause: ObjectMgr::SelectDifficultyInfo (ObjectMgr.cpp:10945) returns nullptr when the exact difficulty row is missing (the only fallbacks are heroic raid -> normal raid,
--   LFR/flex -> 25/10 normal, challenge -> heroic dungeon). Creature::SelectLevel (Creature.cpp:1247) then keeps the template level/Health_mod and
--   Creature::UpdateDamagePhysical (StatSystem.cpp:1262) uses DamageModifier 1.0, so in heroic these creatures hit with 1.0 instead of their fix-29 calibrated normal value
--   (e.g. Vanessa VanCleef 2.656, Jan'alai 3.515, Daakara 2.178, the whole Zul'Gurub/Zul'Aman/End Time/Well of Eternity/Hour of Twilight bosses and elites).
-- Rules (per row, in the trailing comment):
--   A  (31 rows) ref_cpp has a separate heroic template (difficulty_entry_1): level and health_mod from that template (hm = our normal hm x cpp heroic hm / cpp normal hm,
--      the same relation the existing heroic rows have), DamageModifier by the heroic-dm rules: exp 0-2 = cpp heroic DM x cpp base / our base (A1, clamp 0.5-30,
--      A2 placeholder 1.0 -> normal x 1.28, R6 floor 1.28 x normal), exp 3 = K3 0.59 x cpp-derived DM clamped to the Cata band p10-p90 (A3).
--   B  ref_cpp has the entry but NO difficulty_entry_1 = one template for all modes (its heroic spawnMask bit is set in ref_cpp for 241 of 352 such creatures):
--      heroic row = the live normal row (level, health_mod, DamageModifier; already fix-29 calibrated on the same ref_cpp template). Cata dungeon pairs in the live data
--      follow the same convention (per-hit heroic/normal 1.0).
--   B2 (derived) same as B for exp 0-2 elites/bosses, but DamageModifier x 1.28 = lowest ref_cpp heroic/normal ratio of the elite cohort (heroic-dm R2/R6 convention),
--      so no heroic elite hits softer than 1.28 x its normal version.
--   B3 (derived) MoP creatures without any ref_cpp entry: copy of the normal row; live MoP pairs in the same dungeons have heroic DM = normal DM.
-- Left out on purpose (see state/heroic_dm.md, section Vervolg): 57 rows whose normal level is >= 3 below the dungeon heroic level (Deadmines, Shadowfang Keep, ...
--   source conflict: ref_cpp spawns them with that low level), 10 rows with normal DM > 8 (event NPCs, e.g. ToC champions), non-combat entries, rank 0 rows with normal DM 1.0.
-- Source: ref_cpp (Cataclysm Preservation TDB434.22011) creature_template + creature_classlevelstats, our creature_classlevelstats, live creature_template_difficulty (dev, 03-11-2026),
--         Map.dbc / MapDifficulty.dbc (heroic 5-man maps), heroic-dm rules from state/heroic_dm.md (commits 86c9ad52, 63f924a9), fix 29 (the internal notes).
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM `creature_template_difficulty` WHERE `difficulty` = 'DUNGEON_HEROIC' AND `id` IN (<the ids below>); (these ids had no heroic row on 03-11-2026; full script state/hdm/heroic_dm_rollback_12.sql)
-- Repeatable: DELETE of exactly these ids followed by the INSERT.

